## Sprint A — Account safety & data integrity

**Goal:** No silent account-delete failures. GDPR export survives partial server errors. Chunking stays safely off.

| # | Task | Why |
|---|------|-----|
| A1 | `onUserDeleted`: return `{ success, firestoreOk, storageOk, subscriptionCancelled }`; don’t claim full success on partial failure | Real GDPR/billing risk today |
| A2 | Surface `cancelActiveSubscription` failures in delete response + log/metric | Recurring billing may continue after delete |
| A3 | GDPR export: if `gdprServerExport` fails → empty `calendar`/`storageFiles` + warning in payload (not total failure) | Export shouldn’t brick on one callable |
| A4 | Document/guard spatial chunking: keep `spatialChunkingEnabled` default `false`; add comment or feature flag guard in prod | C1/C2 bugs are latent only while flag is off |
| A5 | Tests for A1–A3 (extend `onUserDeleted.test.ts`, GDPR export failure path) | Lock behavior before prod deploy |

**Exit criteria**
- [ ] Delete handler tests cover partial Firestore/Storage/subscription failure
- [ ] GDPR export returns partial data + warning when server export fails
- [ ] `npm run check` green (client + functions)
- [ ] Manual: trigger account delete in emulator/staging → response reflects what actually cleaned up

**Do not start in Sprint A:** chunking wiring, storage overwrite fixes, Cloud Armor scripts.

**Say to start:** *"execute Sprint A"*

