## Sprint C — Storage & billing hardening

**Goal:** Storage limits are trustworthy server-side. Upload guards fail closed. WAF script matches reality.

| # | Task | Why |
|---|------|-----|
| C1 | Storage overwrite: don’t double-count on re-upload (generation metadata or delete-then-upload pattern) | `onObjectFinalized` always increments |
| C2 | `getStorageUsageMb` + `assertStorageWithinLimit`: **fail-closed** on read error (block upload, don’t assume 0 MB) | TOCTOU / fail-open bypass |
| C3 | Refresh storage usage in `useTierLimits` after successful upload | UI can show stale “under limit” |
| C4 | One-time reconciliation script/job: rebuild `usage/storage` from GCS listing | Pre-trigger users may have wrong counters |
| C5 | Fix `setup-cloud-armor.sh`: HTTP callables only; remove event/scheduled triggers; update `cloudArmorCoverage.structural.test.ts` | Misconfigured WAF |
| C6 | `verifyTurnstile` unit tests | Login CAPTCHA path untested |
| C7 | `SubscriptionBillingGroup` + `AccountUsageGroup` component tests | Razorpay vs Stripe UI regressions |

**Exit criteria**
- [ ] Re-upload same file → usage doesn’t inflate
- [ ] Upload blocked when storage read fails (not silently allowed)
- [ ] Cloud Armor structural test matches corrected script
- [ ] `npm run check` green
- [ ] Manual: upload to cap → blocked; delete file → counter drops; Pro user upload works

**Deploy slice (optional end of Sprint C):** deploy `onStorageObject*` + updated rules if not already in prod.

**Say to start:** *"execute Sprint C"*

